Of course!  Loops are a way to repeat a section of code multiple times.  In C, you can use a "for" loop to repeat a section of code a specific number of times.  Here’s an example:

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    doSomething();
}

In this case, "i" is the loop variable, and "n" is the number of times it should loop.  I recommend that you read your programming textbook to learn how loops work in your specific language.  It may also be a good idea to practice writing your own loops in your textbook to reinforce what you’re learning.

